results.evidence:
In pkg/storage/unified/resource/list_with_selectors.go:
```go
	searchFields := s.getSearchFields()
	if searchFields == nil {
		return false
	}

	key := NewLowerGroupResource(req.Options.Key.Group, req.Options.Key.Resource)
	declared := searchFields.SelectableFields(key)
	if len(declared) == 0 {
		return false
	}

	for _, f := range req.Options.Fields {
		name := strings.TrimPrefix(f.Key, SEARCH_SELECTABLE_FIELDS_PREFIX)
		if !slices.Contains(declared, name) {
			return false
		}
	}

	return true
```
The hardcoded manifest check `slices.ContainsFunc(manifests, ...)` was removed and replaced with dynamic verification against `searchFields.SelectableFields(key)`.

In pkg/storage/unified/resource/list_with_selectors.go:
```go
	for _, f := range req.Options.Fields {
		name := strings.TrimPrefix(f.Key, SEARCH_SELECTABLE_FIELDS_PREFIX)
		if !slices.Contains(declared, name) {
			return false
		}
	}

	return true
```
Every field in `req.Options.Fields` is checked against `declared`; if any field is not contained, `shouldUseSearchForList` returns false.

In pkg/storage/unified/resource/list_with_selectors.go:
```go
	if len(declared) == 0 {
		return false
	}

	for _, f := range req.Options.Fields {
		name := strings.TrimPrefix(f.Key, SEARCH_SELECTABLE_FIELDS_PREFIX)
		if !slices.Contains(declared, name) {
			return false
		}
	}
```
When a field is not declared searchable, `shouldUseSearchForList` returns `false`, causing the server to fall back to scanning storage rather than issuing an index query.

In pkg/storage/unified/resource/list_with_selectors.go:
```go
func (s *server) getSearchFields() *SearchFieldsRegistry {
	if s.searchFields != nil {
		return s.searchFields
	}
	return NewSearchFieldsRegistry(SelectableFields(), nil, nil)
}
```
and pkg/storage/unified/resource/server.go:
```go
	sf := opts.SearchFields
	if sf == nil {
		sf = opts.Search.SearchFields
	}
	if sf == nil {
		sf = NewSearchFieldsRegistry(SelectableFields(), nil, nil)
	}
```
When the registry of searchable fields is absent/unset (`s.searchFields == nil`), `getSearchFields` constructs a fallback registry populated with `SelectableFields()`. Consequently, field selectors on built-in kinds present in `SelectableFields()` return `true` and are queried against the search index instead of falling back to storage scan.

